# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# GlassOS client credentials are extracted on-device into app-private storage and must never be
# committed or bundled into a build (see docs/PLAN.md section 2.2). These patterns are a backstop,
# not the mechanism.
*.pem
*.key
# ...but the throwaway test fixture must be committed; it contains generated certs, no secrets.
!apps/spikes/test/fixtures/**
*.p12
*.pfx
certs/
glassos/
# ...but the extracted GlassOS *protocol definitions* are API surface, not secrets, and are the
# whole point of protocol/glassos. Certificates and keys there stay ignored by the *.pem/*.key
# rules above, which is the protection that actually matters.
!protocol/glassos/
!protocol/glassos/**
# Re-assert the credential ban *after* the negation above, because `!protocol/glassos/**` would
# otherwise re-include the very .pem/.key files the rules at the top of this section exist to keep
# out. Verified with `git check-ignore`: protos are committable, credentials are not.
protocol/glassos/**/*.pem
protocol/glassos/**/*.key
protocol/glassos/**/*.p12
protocol/glassos/**/*.pfx
protocol/glassos/**/*.jks
protocol/glassos/**/*.bks
protocol/glassos/**/*.apk

# Captured protocol traces may contain serial numbers and account identifiers. Scrub before
# committing anything under tools/ (docs/PLAN.md section 7).
*.trace
*.pcap
incident-*.log
